arcint (0.2.13-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * M7 fit pass: measured two-ledger reservation; auto-fit of --n-ctx. An
    explicit --n-ctx is verify-only, never lowered, and its refusal now
    trims the prefix-cache reserve pages first. Ship note: the honest
    ledger admits 155,568 tokens (measured with --mtp on) for the dense 27B agent at u8 on the
    24 GB card with an 8 GiB prefix cache, so unit files that hand-set
    155,648 must lower it.
  * --prefix-cache-reserve PCT: under auto-fit, hold PCT percent of the
    affordable KV pages spare for cached prefixes (default 0 = all live
    pages, as before); refused with an explicit --n-ctx, whose reserve is
    whatever remains. Measured: the dense agent at 25% adopts 116,528 with
    2,428 pages spare against 155,376 with none.
  * M8 asymmetric KV, --paged-kv u8:i4 (8.8 vs 11.3 KiB/token; auto-fit
    171,312 vs 133,456 on the coder on the 16 GiB card, 199,424 vs
    155,376 on the agent on the 24 GB card, +28%; acceptance task 10/10
    at u8:i4). Owed: the prefill price, prefix byte-exactness.
  * M9 device-tier expert slot pool plus async uploads: the 35B on the
    16 GiB card goes from 0.4 t/s (ratio 25, unpatched) to 9.1 (ratio 50 /
    8 GiB pool, 16-token probe) and 10.4 (64-token probe).
  * M14 host compute tier, --moe-cpu-tier: the 35B on the 16 GiB card at
    15.0/15.5 t/s against 10.4/10.6 at ratio 50 / 8 GiB, 14.1/14.8
    against 7.4/7.5 at ratio 75 / 5 GiB, text byte-identical, 10/10.
  * M12 --pin-dispatch (measured null on a quiet host, opt-in) and the
    exporter's --moe-lowering tiled.
  * M13 --vision stays reserved and refused; vision IRs are reported at
    load and never loaded (coder: 6 files, 428.3 MiB on disk).
  * Per-expert routing histogram, env MOE_OTD_ROUTING_HIST (plugin patch
    0013).
  * Requires marfrit-openvino +p2.

 -- Markus Fritsche <mfritsche@reauktion.de>  Thu, 03 Sep 2026 10:00:00 +0200

arcint (0.2.12-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * DFlash2 block-diffusion drafter: --dflash DIR serves the public
    Qwen3.8-27B draft head through the checkpoint-row verify, seven drafts
    per pass. Measured on the B60: 44.8 t/s against 24.0 plain and 33.0 with
    the MTP head; --dflash-device parks the draft on the other card with
    byte-identical output (39.8 t/s, 35k tokens more context headroom).
    Greedy-only, one drafter per server. tools/export_dflash.py exports the
    head with the f16 residual-range identities (the raw head peaks at ~128k,
    past f16's 65504); the pairing probe and parity instruments ship in
    tools/.
  * README reordered: build and measurements first; the DFlash2 grid added.

 -- Markus Fritsche <mfritsche@reauktion.de>  Mon, 01 Sep 2026 16:00:00 +0200

arcint (0.2.11-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * The operator serving-defaults layer: --temp, --top-p, --top-k,
    --repetition-penalty, --presence-penalty and
    --chat-template-kwarg enable_thinking=BOOL. Precedence request > flags >
    artifact > family card, each layer overriding only what it sets; any
    sampler flag turns /props' sampler_defaults.provenance to "operator".
    Validation is shared with the request path, so a bad flag refuses at boot
    with the wording a client would get at 400.
  * The performance regime is visible per response:
    usage.completion_tokens_details carries accepted/rejected_prediction_tokens,
    so a caller can see whether speculation engaged instead of reading the log.
  * presence_penalty is now read from the artifact's generation_config.json
    (implemented and request-settable, but silently dropped on load).

